okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Management-only endpoint to push (multiple) API keys, provider, current model and (multiple) OAuth tokens to a host remotely and have them used."
reported: "User, 2026-10-05: '(멀티)api key, 프로바이더, 현재 사용모델, (멀티) oauth 토큰등을 원격에서 푸시하고 액티브하게 사용할수있도록 하는 관리 전용 엔드포인트가 필요'. Choice: on the existing workspace router (not a daemon, not pull)."
design:
  module: "ciel_runtime_support/remote_management_http.py (RemoteManagementController), delegated from web_access_http for /ca/manage/* and wired in ciel_runtime.py on the existing access line (ciel_runtime.py stays at its 4980-line ratchet)."
  routes: "GET /ca/manage/state (provider, model, per-provider API keys as mask+fingerprint, OAuth token rows; no secret values). POST /ca/manage/apply {provider, model, api_keys{provider:{mode replace|append|remove|clear, keys}}, oauth_tokens[{action add|update|remove|refresh, ...}]}."
  semantics: "Whole change set validated first (unknown fields/providers/modes/token ids, credential shape); then provider -> keys -> model -> tokens; any failure restores the saved config (and clears the model cache) and answers 400 changed=false. Existing setters reused: set_provider_choice_config, store_api_keys_config/clear_api_key_config (round-robin), set_model_config ('Model selection rejected' treated as failure), OAuthTokenStore. Audit: workspace management-audit.jsonl with origin, model, provider, key fingerprints, token actions."
  auth: "Router access check unchanged: loopback, admin bearer token (CIEL_RUNTIME_ROUTER_EXTERNAL_TOKEN or the stored token), signed-in web session. From another host the router's external access must be on."
tests:
  unit: "tests/test_remote_management_http.py (8): state hides key values; provider+model+append; remove by fingerprint and clear; rejected model restores provider and keys, no audit; failing key store restores provider; seven invalid change sets change nothing; OAuth add (credential and file content), disable, remove, audit and response free of secrets; web access delegation. Unit group with it: see release entry."
  e2e_router: "evidence/apply-e2e.json: real `ciel_runtime.py serve` (isolated config, provider vllm -> local stub upstream). Before push upstream saw Bearer k-old-1. From the LAN address 172.29.112.1: no token -> 401; admin token -> 200 (keys replaced by 2, model m-new, Claude OAuth token added). Next requests: Bearer k-new-1, k-new-2, k-new-1, k-new-2 (round-robin). Model: requests with alias ciel-runtime-vllm-m-old and with m-old still reached upstream as m-old; alias ciel-runtime-vllm-m-new as m-new. Change set {provider codex-routed, invalid key} -> 400 changed=false, provider stayed vllm, keys unchanged, no audit line. Secret values absent from every management response and the audit."
  e2e_oauth: "evidence/oauth-e2e.json: provider anthropic routed -> stub. Before push upstream saw the CLI's own Bearer sk-ant-oat-local-cli; after pushing a Claude token the next request carried Bearer sk-ant-oat-pushed-e2e."
finding_model: "A running session names its model in every request (the launch alias ciel-runtime-<provider>-<model>), and the router honours it, so changing current_model alone reaches new launches only (first E2E run: alias ciel-runtime-vllm-m-old still went upstream as m-old after pushing m-new)."
model_scope:
  decision: "User, 2026-10-05: force running sessions too ('실행 중 세션도 강제 전환')."
  change: "ciel_runtime_support/model_override.py: provider config forced_model. provider_model_selection.resolve_requested_model resolves forced_model instead of the requested model (tool model references untouched); router_http.forward_json (Codex routed) replaces body.model. Management apply: model_scope running (default with a model) sets forced_model to the selected current_model; launch releases it. A local model choice (menu/CLI set_model) pops forced_model."
  e2e: "evidence/apply-e2e.json (second run): after pushing m-new (running) every request naming ciel-runtime-vllm-m-old or m-old reached upstream as m-new with keys k-new-1/k-new-2 alternating; after {model_scope: launch} the alias went upstream as m-old again; after re-pushing m-new and running `ciel_runtime.py model m-old` locally, forced_model was '' and the request went as m-old."
tests_final: "unit 1737 OK (skipped 49), router 1175 OK, channel 454 OK (skipped 80), runtime 369 OK (skipped 19); ruff clean; docs metadata clean; live router 9611 = 200."
not_done: "Not committed, not pushed, not published. The CLI of a forced running session still shows its launch model name."
